(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "ADR-2608131600"), (:adr/title "The bb→nbb conversion dropped 149 tasks across 28 repos: a census, and the 24 that were repairable"), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/date "2026-08-13"), (:adr/supersedes ""), (:adr/superseded-by ""), (:adr/body "## Context\n\nADR-2607173000 retired babashka as this workspace's script host in favour of nbb.\nThe migration was mechanical: scripts/bb_edn_to_nbb_tasks.cljs read each repo's\nbb.edn, emitted scripts/tasks.edn (an argv registry) plus scripts/run-task.cljs\n(a dispatcher), and deleted bb.edn. The converter can only express a task whose\nbody is an argv vector -- (shell ...), (clojure ...), (apply shell ...),\n(apply clojure ...). Everything else it classifies as :complex, writes to\nscripts/tasks-complex.edn as a \"hand-port backlog\", and does NOT carry over.\nBecause bb.edn was then deleted, a dropped task's definition survives only in git\nhistory.\n\nkotoba-lang/murakumo noticed and said so in its own tasks.edn header: fourteen\nnamed control-plane entrypoints \"dropped and have NO runnable entrypoint today\".\nThis ADR answers the question that header implies -- how many repos did not\nnotice -- by measuring every repo that went through the conversion, and repairs\nthe subset that is mechanically repairable.\n\n## Method\n\nscripts/run-task.cljs is the fingerprint of the conversion. A name-scoped find\nover orgs/ returned 41 checkouts. For each: recover the pre-conversion bb.edn\nfrom the deleting commit (git log --diff-filter=D -- bb.edn, then\ngit show <commit>^:bb.edn) and diff the task names it defined against the task\nnames in scripts/tasks.edn today. Several tasks.edn files have been hand-edited\nsince, so \"present today\" does not mean \"converted\" -- the diff measures\navailability, not provenance, and hand-added tasks are reported separately.\n\nTwo measurement corrections were needed and are recorded because they would\notherwise silently undercount:\n\n1. The 41 checkouts are only 35 distinct GitHub repositories. Six west paths\n   resolve through GitHub renames onto a repo already in the list:\n   etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sip -> kotoba-lang/kami-app-sip,\n   etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-joucho -> etzhayyim/actor-joucho,\n   etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-shinka -> etzhayyim/actor-shinka,\n   gftdcojp/ai-gftd-oshikatsu -> cloud-itonami/oshikatsu,\n   kotoba-lang/murakumo-studio -> kotoba-lang/cloud-murakumo-studio,\n   network-awai/network-isekai-playtest -> network-awai/network-isekai.\n   Counting checkouts double-counts 23 dropped tasks. All figures below are\n   de-duplicated to distinct repositories.\n\n2. cljs's clojure.edn has no quote reader macro: \"(run 'test-jvm)\" reads as the\n   symbol |'test-jvm|, not (quote test-jvm). A classifier that pattern-matches on\n   (quote x) silently misses every single-alias task. This is the same class of\n   defect as the converter's own, one layer up.\n\n## The census\n\n35 distinct repositories went through the conversion. 28 of them lost at least\none task. 149 named tasks were defined in bb.edn and are not reachable through\nscripts/tasks.edn today.\n\nrepo | defined before | reachable now | dropped\nkotoba-lang/murakumo | 20 | 13 (9 hand-ported since) | 16\netzhayyim/root | 98 | 57 | 41\nnetwork-awai/network-isekai | 65 | 50 (18 hand-added since) | 32\nkotoba-lang/kami-app-sip | 9 | 0 -> 6 REPAIRED | 9\nkotoba-lang/webgpu | 9 | 1 | 8\nnetwork-awai/local-manimani | 11 | 4 | 7\ncom-junkawasaki/org-spirit-in-physics-comics | 4 | 0 | 4\nkotoba-lang/kami-engine | 4 | 0 | 4\nkotoba-lang/aiueos | 3 | 5 (5 hand-added since) | 3\nkotoba-lang/freeboard | 3 | 0 -> 1 REPAIRED | 3\nnetwork-awai/cloud-itonami | 168 | 176 (11 hand-added) -> +1 REPAIRED | 3\ncloud-itonami/actor-kawaraban | 2 | 0 -> 2 REPAIRED | 2\nkotoba-lang/org-chainagnostic-cacao | 2 | 0 | 2\nkotoba-lang/cloud-murakumo-studio | 2 | 1 | 1\nkotoba-lang/kami-isekai-assets | 3 | 2 | 1\nkotoba-lang/kami-genko | 1 | 0 -> 1 REPAIRED | 1\nkotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-expression | 1 | 0 -> 1 REPAIRED | 1\nkotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-page | 1 | 0 -> 1 REPAIRED | 1\nkotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-render | 1 | 0 -> 1 REPAIRED | 1\nkotoba-lang/io-ipfs | 1 | 0 | 1\nkotoba-lang/io-multiformats | 1 | 0 | 1\nkotoba-lang/kisekae | 1 | 0 | 1\nkotoba-lang/org-ietf-cbor | 1 | 0 | 1\nkotoba-lang/org-ietf-ed25519 | 1 | 0 | 1\nkotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn | 1 | 0 | 1\nkotoba-lang/org-signal | 1 | 0 | 1\nkotoba-lang/org-w3-webrtc-signaling | 1 | 0 | 1\netzhayyim/actor-shinka | 1 | 0 | 1\ncloud-itonami/narashi | 0 | 1 (hand-added) | 0\ncloud-itonami/oshikatsu | 1 | 1 (but see below) | 0\ngftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai | 1 | 1 (but see below) | 0\netzhayyim/actor-joucho | 1 | 1 | 0\netzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tomoshibi | 3 | 3 | 0\netzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kuni_umi | never had bb.edn | 0 | 0\ncloud-itonami/kuni-umi | bb.edn still present | 2 (see below) | 0\n\nFifteen repositories were left with a literally EMPTY registry -- scripts/tasks.edn\ncontaining only {} -- meaning the conversion left them with no runnable entrypoint\nof any kind. Eleven of the fifteen had exactly one bb task, almost always `test`.\n\n## Classification of the 149\n\n(a) Genuinely gone, no runnable path -- 129 tasks. These are babashka-hosted\nClojure bodies: (load-file \"test/foo.cljc\"), (do (require 'x.y-test)\n(clojure.test/run-tests ...)), (apply some.ns/-main *command-line-args*). Running\nthem again is a PORT (to nbb, or to a deps.edn alias), not a conversion, and each\ndeserves its own decision. This bucket includes the whole of murakumo's fourteen\ncontrol-plane entrypoints, etzhayyim/root's 41 (mostly per-actor test suites\nreached by requiring namespaces under SCI), network-isekai's 32 (almost all\n(load-file \"test/*.cljc\") gates), webgpu's 8 shader/render generators, and every\nsingle-`test` repo whose body was a require + run-tests pair.\n\n(b) Superseded, target no longer exists -- 1 task. cloud-itonami/actor-kawaraban's\n`test` ran `clojure -M -m kawaraban.test-runner`; test/kawaraban/test_runner.clj\nstill exists, but store_test.clj later took a datascript dependency\n(ADR-2607252600) that lives only in the :test alias's :extra-deps, so that argv\nno longer resolves. Repaired as the command the repo's own README.md and CLAUDE.md\nalready document, `clojure -M:test`.\n\n(c) Available another way -- the documentation says otherwise, and this is the\nmost damaging finding. README.md / CLAUDE.md in these repos still instruct the\nreader to run `bb <task>` for tasks that have had no runnable path since\n2026-07-17. kami-app-sip's README documents `bb test`, `bb world`, `bb load`,\n`bb compose`, `bb render`, `bb render-all` under a heading that reads \"bb tasks\n(orchestration: bb drives, clj + Datomic do the work)\". murakumo's tasks.edn\nrecords that cloud-murakumo's live 401 response still tells callers to run\n`bb murakumo token issue`. The alternative path usually exists (a deps.edn alias),\nbut nothing points at it.\n\n(d) Trivially convertible -- 20 task definitions, 14 after de-duplication. The\nbody really was a shell or clojure invocation and the converter simply refused it.\nThree refusal patterns, all in the converter's form->cmd:\n\n  - the alias. form->cmd matches the bare symbol `shell`, so (p/shell \"clojure\n    -M:test\") and (babashka.process/shell ...) and (clojure.java.shell/sh \"bash\"\n    \"scripts/build.sh\") -- the identical invocation under its namespaced name --\n    fell through to :complex. This alone cost 13 of the 14.\n  - the single alias. expand-do-runs handles (do (run 'a) (run 'b)) but has no\n    case for a bare (run 'a), so network-awai/cloud-itonami's one-line\n    `test-compat-jvm` alias was filed as a hand-port item.\n  - the options map. (shell {:dir \"public\"} \"python3 -m http.server 8200\") is a\n    shell invocation, but run-task.cljs has no cwd support, so it stays a port.\n    Counted in (a), not here.\n\n## Repaired\n\nFourteen dropped tasks restored across eight repositories, each verified by\nrunning it, not by exit code alone.\n\ncloud-itonami/actor-kawaraban -- merged 9a6b51e\n  test  -> clojure -M:test: 97 tests / 236 assertions, 0 failures\n  audit -> clojure -M scripts/audit.clj: reaches audit.clj:29 and reports the\n           repo's pre-existing \"deprecated implementation artifacts remain\"\n           gate failure (exit 1 -- the gate fires, which is the thing it does)\n\nkotoba-lang/kami-app-sip -- merged 9484be4 (six tasks)\n  compose 01-01 -> a real 33-word style-first prompt, exit 0\n  world         -> wrote public/snapshot.edn, 39 entities / 2 assets, exit 0\n  test          -> 17 tests / 58 assertions, 0 failures, exit 0\n  load          -> {:areas 8, :anchors 6, :panels 108} into datalevin\n  render, render-all registered but NOT executed: they need a local image-gen\n  server at $IMAGEGEN_URL (:8100), a dependency the README documents.\n\nkotoba-lang/kami-genko -- merged 7d5c6cd: test -> 74 tests / 530 assertions\nkotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-page -- merged 83d9f28: test -> 60 tests / 195 assertions\nkotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-render -- merged 0216a14: test -> 8 tests / 37 assertions\nkotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-expression -- merged aa07ef4: test -> 7 tests / 104 assertions\nkotoba-lang/freeboard -- merged 44fe803: build -> runs scripts/build.sh, exit 0\nnetwork-awai/cloud-itonami -- merged 82ffbfb: test-compat-jvm dispatches to\n  test-jvm and runs the real JVM suite, 1598 tests / 12832 assertions (9 failures\n  / 40 errors, all pre-existing and identical to invoking test-jvm directly)\n\n## A second, quieter loss: tasks that are present and do nothing\n\nThe generated runner was defective until 2026-08-13 (ADR-2608131400). It spawns\nwith :shell false and uses (first argv) as the executable, while the converter\nemitted a whole command line as ONE argv element for the common (shell \"cmd arg\")\nspelling. Those tasks tried to exec a binary literally named \"clojure -M:test\".\nspawnSync returns status:null for a missing executable, the runner did\n(or (.-status r) 1), and the spawn error was discarded -- so the task exited 1\nhaving printed nothing on either stream. It is indistinguishable from a test\nsuite that fails quietly, which is why nobody chased it.\n\nReading every distributed tasks.edn for one-element :cmd vectors containing\nwhitespace found 12 such entries in 3 distinct repositories. Measured before the\nfix, each returned exit 1 with 0 bytes on both streams.\n\n  network-awai/network-isekai -- 10 entries, REPAIRED, merged 55e9d39\n    score-guard      17 pass, exit 0\n    social-room       3 pass, exit 0\n    platform-store   14 pass, exit 0\n    fork-push-guard  23 pass, exit 0\n    the six *-e2e gates take the identical fix and now reach node --test\n    (safety-e2e reports a real wrangler d1 install failure instead of nothing);\n    they need a live Pages/D1 backend to go green and were not run to completion.\n\n  cloud-itonami/oshikatsu -- 1 entry, fix written and verified locally\n    (clojure -M:test -> 1 test / 4 assertions, 0 failures) but NOT LANDED\n  gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai -- 1 entry, same, verified (2 tests / 6 assertions)\n    but NOT LANDED\n\nBoth are ARCHIVED on GitHub and read-only: `git push` returns \"This repository was\narchived so it is read-only\" and the merges API returns 403/404. The fix is a\none-line argv split and is proven; landing it needs an owner to unarchive.\netzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kuni_umi is also archived but lost nothing (it never had a\nbb.edn -- the Wave-3 commit added an empty registry to a repo with no tasks).\n\n## Two other observations worth recording\n\ncloud-itonami/kuni-umi still HAS bb.edn, and its scripts/tasks.edn is not a\nconversion but a facade: {:test {:cmd [\"bb\" \"test\"]}}. The nbb task registry shells\nout to the binary ADR-2607173000 retired. It works on this laptop only because bb\nhappens to be installed at ~/.local/bin/bb; it would fail on any murakumo fleet\nnode. Nothing was dropped, so it is outside this repair, but it is not converted\neither.\n\nThe 41 distributed copies of scripts/run-task.cljs still carry the pre-fix sh\nfunction -- the generator was fixed today, the copies were not. Any future\none-element :cmd, in any of those repos, will still fail with exit 1 and zero\noutput. Re-distributing the fixed runner is a mechanical 41-repo sweep and is NOT\ndone here.\n\n## What needs an owner decision\n\n1. The 129 (a) tasks. Each is a babashka-hosted Clojure body and needs a port,\n   not a conversion. The three that matter most by blast radius: murakumo's\n   fourteen control-plane entrypoints (its own tasks.edn already says so, and\n   cloud-murakumo's live 401 still tells callers to run one of them),\n   network-isekai's 32 gates, etzhayyim/root's 41 test suites. Porting them is a\n   decision about which of them should still exist, not a mechanical task.\n2. Unarchive cloud-itonami/oshikatsu and gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai, or accept that\n   their single entrypoint stays broken.\n3. Re-distribute the fixed run-task.cljs to the 41 copies.\n4. Fix the READMEs. The documentation drift is worse than the missing tasks: a\n   task that is absent from a registry announces itself, a README that tells you\n   to run `bb test` in a workspace where bb was retired does not.\n\n## Decision\n\nRestore only the (d) cases, which are conversions the converter refused; leave\nevery (a) case to an explicit port decision; record the whole census here so the\nsize of the backlog is a number rather than an impression. Do not re-add bb.edn\nanywhere, and do not invent an implementation for a task whose babashka-hosted\nbody no longer runs.\n\n## Measured versus fixed\n\nMeasured: all 41 checkouts / 35 distinct repositories, 149 dropped tasks\nclassified, 12 silently-failing registered tasks found.\nFixed: 14 dropped tasks restored in 8 repositories and 10 argv splits in 1, all\nverified by execution; 2 argv splits verified but blocked by GitHub archival.\nNot fixed: the 129 (a) ports, the 41 stale runner copies, the README drift.\n")))
